      "content": "The only way to truly fix a broken tree is to prune the dead parts so it can survive, not to wipe your existence entirely. If you leave, you aren't actually cleaning up the stain, you are just erasing the person who makes you who you are and condemning yourself to a lonely, guarded past. Sometimes the most honorable thing is to stay, confront the pain, and explain that you cannot let your family's pride get in the way of their own peace. A legacy built on perfection that requires your erasure to exist is one that never belonged to begin with.",
